00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.520
Here in North America, way up in the Arctic tundra,

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.620
where the winter winds blow cold, snow and ice cover the ground,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.100
and the temperatures fall way below freezing.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.800
It's us, the Krat Brothers.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.640
I'm Chris.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.830
I'm Martin.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.000
And if you're a creature trying to survive in the tundra, you have to have some

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.740
some serious cold weather adaptations.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:39.460
And there's one animal who definitely has what it takes.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.950
These are musk oxen,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.290
the amazing shaggy powerhouses of the North.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.110
Oh, and I love that shaggy fur.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:50.710
It's a long, very cool face on these creatures.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.710
A long, slopey face with those characteristic horns

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.450
that swoop down and out.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.000
Musk ox live in herds, groups of about 10 to 20

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.480
oxen. They're made of males, females, and young, and everybody has to get along. That's because

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:11.860
living together is vital. Partly for protection from predators like arctic wolves, and partly

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:18.620
to help deal with the cold winter. After a snowfall, you'll find muskoxen covered in snow.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.570
They don't mind. That shaggy fur keeps them worn. Hey, and the snow just gives extra insulation.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.470
But when they get up, the snow gets shaken off.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.000
They don't even care about this.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.230
of snow and cold, but when it gets really cold,

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:35.830
the muskoxen have to huddle together

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.710
to help keep each other warm

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:40.700
and to help block the wind from one another.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.320
So, how do these creatures survive?

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.480
What are the coldest environments on Earth?

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.360
What creature powers do they have,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.720
