00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:36.600
Me!

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:40.090
Oh, come on, Zack.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.890
That collection means nothing to you, but it means a lot to me.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:47.090
It's full of reminders of our really great adventures.

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.240
And our creature friends.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:53.100
Like that piece of shed fur from one of Kid Muskie's herd members.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.460
And a baby tooth from a little arctic wolf pup.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:58.120
Our pal, Baby Tooth.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:59.830
Please, just give it back.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:04.110
I've got your baby tooth. Wah, wah, wah!

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:11.570
You want me to give it back so you can just activate Arctic Wolf powers whenever you want and get in my way?

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:15.350
Never! The collection is mine now!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:21.300
Well, maybe we don't need to activate Arctic Wolf powers.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.000
Wolves?

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:33.170
Zack, meet Baby Tooth's back!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:38.290
They seem interested in you, Zack.

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:41.720
You kind of look like a muskox in that furry jacket.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:58.420
Let's protect him, sir!

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.360
Watch me make my smooth getaway.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:10.440
Snorting at ya, shaggy cow.

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:11.420
You.

00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:14.560
I think he wants to battle you, Zack.

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:15.560
Ah!

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:20.390
Ah!

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:32.910
I can't end your silly soup into your collection.

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:37.930
I really didn't want it any-

00:22:37.930 --> 00:22:44.430
Thanks, Baby Tooth.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:48.290
That's a creature mission accomplished.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:22:55.200
Well, there they go.

00:22:55.920 --> 00:22:59.040
A couple of really cool arctic creatures.

00:22:59.650 --> 00:23:00.000
With them.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.990
awesome creature powers

00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:08.480
See you later, baby tooth. Bye kid musky. Thanks for helping me get my creature souvenir collection back. Oh

00:23:09.460 --> 00:23:11.460
We'll never forget you guys

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:21.920
But they're forgetting us wait

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:24.390
Hey, no problem, bro

00:23:24.390 --> 00:23:30.000
Remember that harpy eagle feather we were looking for cool then we'll

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.870
we'll just catch up.

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:39.440
Activate Harpy Eagle Powers!

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:41.620
Let's fly!

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:51.090
So, the mighty musk oxen of the northern tundra

00:23:51.090 --> 00:23:53.590
have some serious head-butting power.

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:57.100
Yeah, they are one of the most impressive cold-weather creatures

00:23:57.100 --> 00:23:59.100
in the entire creature world.

00:23:59.100 --> 00:24:00.000
And let's get back here.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:08.570
Oh, musk oxen are faster than you might think.

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:11.550
They can run up to 30 miles per hour.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:17.100
But musk oxen don't run very far or very long.

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:20.870
That's because they're designed for hunkering down

00:24:20.870 --> 00:24:23.610
in this snowy, cold climate.

00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:25.310
They have to preserve heat.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:27.560
So when they start running, they overheat quickly.

00:24:27.560 --> 00:24:30.000
They're definitely short-distance runners.

00:24:30.410 --> 00:24:39.640
But it's enough to get a running start for one of those awesome head-butting battles!

00:24:39.640 --> 00:24:43.130
Like two freight trains colliding!

00:24:43.130 --> 00:24:44.890
Check out that thick coat of fur.

00:24:44.890 --> 00:24:49.290
The outer coat never stops growing, and it's the first line of defense for blocking the

00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:51.730
cold wind.

00:24:51.730 --> 00:24:56.510
Underneath the long coat, there's a short, fleecy layer of fur that helps keep them warm.

00:24:56.510 --> 00:25:00.000
They can withstand temperatures way below freezing.

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:03.800
Those feet also have creature powers.

00:25:03.800 --> 00:25:11.310
Sometimes in the winter, the only way to get to food is to crack through the ice and snow,

00:25:11.310 --> 00:25:17.460
and they use their sharp hooves to get down in there, to paw away the snow, and to get

00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:20.910
to the grass and moss and lichen underneath.

00:25:20.910 --> 00:25:23.210
And check out this little guy.

00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:25.820
This is a baby musk ox.

00:25:25.820 --> 00:25:30.000
He's only about four months old, and already pretty big, with an hour

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.020
Hours after a muskox is born, he's up on his feet and ready to keep up with the herd.

00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:37.770
Now that's a pretty cool creature power for a baby.

00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:43.090
The first year's the toughest for the muskox, and he has to stay close to the herd, and

00:25:43.090 --> 00:25:48.990
in the winter, he even hides under his mom's skirt during the really cold days.

00:25:48.990 --> 00:25:54.520
Right, little buddy?

00:25:54.520 --> 00:25:56.420
Keep on creature adventuring.

00:25:56.420 --> 00:25:58.200
We'll see you on the creature trail.

